        -:   18:// Queue Manager — Data Structure Layer (SADS §2, §4).
        -:   19://
        -:   20:// Owns one FIFO queue per lane and is the only component allowed to change
        -:   21:// queue contents. Every operation that could corrupt queue state is refused
        -:   22:// instead of attempted (SADS §10):
        -:   23://   - unknown lane ID          -> rejected, nothing changes
        -:   24://   - dequeue on empty queue   -> returns false, nothing changes
        -:   25://   - vehicle ID already used   -> rejected, so a vehicle is never duplicated
        -:   26://
        -:   27:// Requirements: FR2 (maintain queues), FR5 (entry/exit), FR7 (queue length
        -:   28:// for congestion), NFR1 (O(1) enqueue/dequeue/length), NFR3 and SR2
        -:   29:// (no loss, duplication or corruption of vehicles).
