        -:  127:// Vehicle Manager — Traffic Management Layer (SADS §4).
        -:  128://
        -:  129:// Creates vehicles and moves them into and out of lane queues according to
        -:  130:// the traffic rules (FR1, FR5). All queue changes go through the Queue
        -:  131:// Manager, so its integrity checks (SR2, NFR3) always apply.
        -:  132://
        -:  133:// Traffic rules:
        -:  134://   Entry: a valid vehicle may join a lane in any signal state. It always
        -:  135://          joins the back of that lane's queue.
        -:  136://   Exit:  only the front vehicle of a lane may leave, and only while that
        -:  137://          lane's signal is GREEN. On RED or YELLOW it stays queued (TC-04).
        -:  138:enum class MoveResult {
        -:  139:    Moved,           // front vehicle left the lane
        -:  140:    BlockedBySignal, // lane is RED or YELLOW, nothing changed
        -:  141:    QueueEmpty       // lane is GREEN but has no vehicles, nothing changed
        -:  142:};
